Objective of the game:
Slay 3 monsters or fill your party with a certain number of unique Heroes.
Slaying Monsters:
    Each Monster card has a Hero requirement. The H symbol represents a hero of any class. Otherwise it requires a specific Hero class. When you attack, it costs two action points to attack. Then, you roll two dice. If the sum is greater than or equal to the green number on the monster card, the following effect occurs (most of the time it will be slaying the monster). If your roll is equal to or less than the red number, the listed effect occurs. Generally, losing the roll makes you discard cards from your hand or sacrifice a hero. If your roll is too low, you can use a Modifier card to increase your roll. Your opponents can use their Modifier cards to lower your roll. Most modifiers have a positive and negative number. The user gets to choose which one to use. Modifiers can be played after any roll and can be stacked with other Modifiers.
Winning with Heroes:
    Depending on how many Expansions you have, the amount of heroes you need changes. In the base game, you need 6. If you get 5 unique heroes on your party and your leader is a different class (meaning you have 1 of every class in your party), you win. Your opponents can prevent you by winning like this with cards that change the class of your hero or stealing, sacrificing, or destroying your heroes.
Setup: 
    At the start of the game, the deck is shuffled and every player chooses a Party Leader. Each leader has a unique effect that applies differently throughout the game. Every player draws 5 cards from the deck. Note that the deck used is shared by all players. One player goes first and players take turns in order. When you start your turn, you start with 3 Action Points. Action Points can be spent doing the following: Draw 1 card for 1 AP, Play a card from your hand for 1 AP, activate a Hero effect for 1 AP, Attack a Monster for 2 AP, Discard your hand and draw 5 cards for 3 AP.
    The first thing you want to start doing is getting Heroes in your party. When you play a Hero from your hand, you spend 1 AP and then place it on your Party. If any player has a Challenge card, they can use it to Challenge your summon. Both players roll 2 dice and the higher roller wins. If the challenging player wins, the Hero card gets discarded.